# Drafted by Gemini (R11c bad_seed), edited.

~ morgan_apples
Narrator: A split russet apple sits on the counter, weeping black syrup that smells of burnt sugar and iron.
morgan [sad]: Half the square is abed since the picnic, feverish and coughing up bitter rind. The sickness is in the fruit, and my draughts only slow it.
quest bad_seed sick
* How bad is the sickness? -> morgan_bad
* Where did these apples come from? -> morgan_marl
* We will go to the orchard and end this. -> morgan_go

~ morgan_bad
morgan [weary]: Folks are withering like frost-bitten clover. If the root is not cut soon, the frail ones will not rise.
-> morgan_apples

~ morgan_marl
morgan [sad]: Cecil Marl brought four barrels from his orchard, with comb honey and sweet cream. Barren all last year, his trees now groan with red fruit.
-> morgan_apples

~ morgan_go
morgan [neutral]: Follow the east lane past the hedgerows toward the smell of overripe cider and sulfur. Watch yourselves in his house; no honest harvest turns the core to ash.
quest bad_seed orchard
-> END

~ cecil
Narrator: Sweat gleams on Cecil's cold cheeks, and something small and leathery scratches inside the wainscoting.
cecil_marl [smile]: Come in out of the damp, friends, and try a dipper of sweet press! I cannot help it if my boughs are blessed while the moor goes hungry.
* [Insight DC 14] We know about the pact you made for this harvest. -> cecil_know | cecil_deny
* Why has your fruit made the whole village sick? -> cecil_deny
* Draw your weapon. Your orchard is finished. -> cecil_fight

~ cecil_know
cecil_marl [afraid]: I only signed for golden boughs and a full cellar, I never asked who paid! Stay back, or my little helpers will peel you to the bone!
-> cecil_fight

~ cecil_deny
cecil_marl [sly]: Sickness? Village bellies are just too weak for rich cream and cellar cider.
-> cecil

~ cecil_fight
cecil_marl [angry]: Tear them apart, my beauties, and throw their bones under the roots!
combat wm_bad_seed

~ cured
Narrator: Outside, the red apples shrivel to gray ash on the boughs, and the sour heat breaks like a fever.
morgan [smile]: The village breathes easy again, and the children are asking for broth. Whatever foul bargain fed those roots has gone back to the pit with its master.
quest bad_seed cured
set seed_done
-> END
